really interesting update from Germany's  new defense minister he's only been  officially in the job for one day and  today he was defending his country I'll  just go through some of the points that  he made he has literally just finished  finished speaking in the last minute or  so so he said it was wrong to give the  impression that Germany was standing in  the way but as you said he said that  they were basically weighing up the pros  and cons of sending those tanks and that  they needed to look at things like the  number of stocks and how those tanks  would be sent and time and Logistics and  that while they were doing that he said  they had no problem that Partners did  that as well they said he said that they  also discussed about Partners exporting  their own stocks no decision on that yet  but it he's very keen to make this point  that they aren't standing in the way I  think the other thing that was really  important was that he started his whole  conference to the Press by listing some  of the things that Germany has done so  he underlined the fact that they're  going to send and these murder fighting  Vehicles 40 of those due to be delivered  by March also underlining that they're  sending other support really trying to  make the point clear that Germany is by  no means letting the side down when it  comes to supporting Ukraine but also  underlining that point that many  analysts have said to me over the last  few days that feeling that they really  need to be cautious when they take this  next step of sending in these battle  tanks and he said that um when they're  looking at the pros and cons they had to  balance the pros and cons in the  interest of Europe and the German  population and I think that's a really  interesting point because as we've been  talking today there has been this idea  that the chancellor for example is very  concerned about making wrong decisions  and making decisions very carefully to  ensure that if they send these tanks for  example that it doesn't lead to an  escalation in the war and that is a  point that seems to be supported by a  majority of the German public who in  recent polls by public TV the majority  of them didn't support sending the  leopard tanks leopard two tanks they  said that they did support Ukraine but  this seems to be for many people a step  too far so caution again on the part of  Germany here people who were hoping for  a big announcement today were sending  the tanks that clearly doesn't sound  like it's going to happen What will be  interesting now is to see whether what's  been discussed behind closed doors is  enough to appease Partners like Poland  who are really getting frustrated and  have already already threatened to send  their stocks of these Leopard 2 tanks  without permission
 

